      ],
      "summary": "**Purpose**  \nThe table summarizes the capital structure and key attributes of the Silverbrook CLO 2026‑1 synthetic transaction.\n\n**Key Information**\n\n- **Issuer & Manager**  \n  - Issuer: *Silverbrook Funding Ltd.*  \n  - Collateral Manager: *Silverbrook Asset Management*  \n\n- **Timing**  \n  - Closing Date: **November 12, 2026**  \n  - Reinvestment End: **December 20, 2031**  \n\n- **Target Portfolio**  \n  - Total: **$650,000,000**  \n\n- **Capital Structure (by class)**  \n  | Class | Amount | Rating | Coupon / Spread |\n  |-------|--------|--------|-----------------|\n  | A‑1 | $410,000,000 | AAA / Aaa | 3 m SOFR + 1.55 % |\n  | A‑2 | $52,000,000 | AAA / Aaa | 3 m SOFR + 1.85 % |\n  | B | $48,000,000 | AA / Aa2 | 3 m SOFR + 2.35 % |\n  | C | $35,000,000 | A / A2 | 3 m SOFR + 3.60 % |\n  | D | $25,000,000 | BBB / Baa3 | 3 m SOFR + 5.10 % |\n  | E | $20,000,000 | BB / Ba3 | 3 m SOFR + 8.25 % |\n  | Subordinated | $60,000,000 | NR | Residual |\n\n- **Total Notes Issued**: $610 M (sum of Classes A‑1 through E)  \n- **Subordinated Residual**: $60 M\n\n**Notable Insights**\n\n- The **Class A‑1** notes represent the largest tranche at **$410 M** and carry the highest rating (AAA/Aaa) with the lowest coupon spread (1.55 % above 3 m SOFR).  \n- Coupon spreads **increase progressively** with lower credit ratings, culminating in the **Class E** notes at **8.25 %** above 3 m SOFR.  \n- All tranches are tied to the 3 m SOFR benchmark, indicating a floating‑rate structure.  \n- The **Subordinated** tranche is labeled “NR” (non‑rated) and is designated as residual, implying it absorbs losses after senior tranches.  \n- The **Target Portfolio** of $650 M exceeds the sum of the senior tranches ($610 M) by $40 M, which aligns with the subordinated residual tranche of $60 M, suggesting a cushion for credit losses.  \n\nThis concise snapshot captures the transaction’s structure, timing, and credit hierarchy, providing a clear reference for stakeholders and analysts."
    }
